  "layout_note": "Preface incipit. Ornamental floral woodcut headpiece (border art, ignored) across the top; 4-line display heading in roman capitals; ornamental woodcut drop-cap 'A' opening the prose (text wraps to its right for 5 lines). Single wide prose column with two small ROMAN side-notes in the right margin. Second paragraph ('If anie demand...') opens with a faint paragraph/pilcrow mark in the left margin (not transcribed into text). Foot bears signature '†2' (cross-shaped mark) centered and catchword 'we' at right. Language: English, period orthography. w/vv is per-glyph on this page (see notes).",
  "body": [
    {"line_index": 0, "role": "title_display", "text": "TO THE RIGHT;"},
    {"line_index": 1, "role": "title_display", "text": "VVELBELOVED ENGLISH"},
    {"line_index": 2, "role": "title_display", "text": "READER GRACE AND GLORIE"},
    {"line_index": 3, "role": "title_display", "text": "IN IESVS CHRIST EVERLASTING."},

    {"line_index": 4, "role": "drop_cap", "text": "A", "note": "ornamental woodcut initial; reads with the following small-caps 'T LAST' as 'AT LAST'"},

    {"line_index": 5, "role": "prose", "text": "T LAST through Gods goodnes(moſt dearly", "note": "'T LAST' set in small capitals after the drop-cap A"},
    {"line_index": 6, "role": "prose", "text": "beloued) we ſend you here the greater part"},
    {"line_index": 7, "role": "prose", "text": "of the Old Teſtament: as long ſince you re-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 8, "role": "prose", "text": "ceiued the New ; faithfully tranſlated into"},
    {"line_index": 9, "role": "prose", "text": "English. The reſidue is in hãd to be finiſhed:", "note": "'hãd' = 'hand' with tilde/nasal abbreviation over the a, as printed. GLYPH-DRIVEN s-mix on this line: 'English' uses ROUND s (short curvy s, verified at high zoom), while 'reſidue' and 'finiſhed' use long-ſ; colon after 'finiſhed' is tight (no French space)."},

    {"line_index": 10, "role": "prose", "text": "and your deſire therof shal not now (God proſpering our"},
    {"line_index": 11, "role": "prose", "text": "intention) be long fruſtrate. As for the impediments, which"},
    {"line_index": 12, "role": "prose", "text": "hitherto haue hindered this vvorke, they al proceded (as"},
    {"line_index": 13, "role": "prose", "text": "manie do know)of one general cauſe, our poore eſtate in"},
    {"line_index": 14, "role": "prose", "text": "banishment. VVherin expecting better meanes,greatter"},
    {"line_index": 15, "role": "prose", "text": "difficulties rather enſued. Neuertheles you wil hereby the"},
    {"line_index": 16, "role": "prose", "text": "more perceiue our feruent good wil,euer to ſerue you, in"},
    {"line_index": 17, "role": "prose", "text": "that we haue brought forth this Tome, in theſe hardeſt"},
    {"line_index": 18, "role": "prose", "text": "times, of aboue fourtie yeares, ſince this College was moſt"},
    {"line_index": 19, "role": "prose", "text": "happely begune. VVherfore we nothing doubt, but you"},
    {"line_index": 20, "role": "prose", "text": "our deareſt, for whom we haue dedicated our liues, wil"},
    {"line_index": 21, "role": "prose", "text": "both pardon the long delay, which we could not wel pre-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 22, "role": "prose", "text": "uent, and accept now this fruict of our laboures, with like"},
    {"line_index": 23, "role": "prose", "text": "good affection, as we acknowlege them due, and offer"},
    {"line_index": 24, "role": "prose", "text": "the ſame vnto you."},

    {"line_index": 25, "role": "prose", "text": "If anie demand, why it is now allowed to haue the holie", "note": "paragraph opens with a faint pilcrow/paragraph mark set in the left margin"},
    {"line_index": 26, "role": "prose", "text": "Scriptures in vulgar tongues, which generally is not per-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 27, "role": "prose", "text": "mitted, but in the three ſacred only:for further declaration"},
    {"line_index": 28, "role": "prose", "text": "of this, & other like pointes we remite you to the Preface,"},
    {"line_index": 29, "role": "prose", "text": "before the New Teſtament.Only here, as by an Epitome,"},

    {"line_index": 30, "role": "signature", "text": "†2", "note": "cross/dagger-shaped signature mark with figure 2, centered at foot"},
    {"line_index": 31, "role": "catchword", "text": "we", "note": "catchword at foot-right anticipating first word of next page; excluded from prose concatenation"}
  ],
